---
// Learner's permit to full license (#594, part of #273): West Virginia's
// graduated driver licensing in three levels, from the DMV's GDL page, and
// the Morgantown DMV office. Every rule here is on the DMV page read
// October 30, 2026: https://dmv.wv.gov/graduated-drivers-licensing-gdl
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ResourceCard from '../components/ResourceCard.astro';
import { loadDir } from '../lib/content.mjs';
import { fixFormUrl } from '../lib/group-requests.mjs';
export const page = { door: "family", topic: "family", label: "Teen drivers: permit to full license", summary: "West Virginia's three steps for drivers under 18: ages, hours, passenger and night limits, and fees" };
const all = loadDir('resources');
const r = (slug) => all.find((e) => e.slug === slug);
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const gdl = 'https://dmv.wv.gov/graduated-drivers-licensing-gdl';
---
<Base title="Teen drivers in Morgantown and Mon County: learner's permit to full license" description="West Virginia's graduated driver licensing for teens, in three levels: the instruction permit at 15, the intermediate license at 16, and the full license at 17, with hours, passenger and night limits and fees, plus the Morgantown DMV office.">
  <h1>Teen drivers: permit to full license</h1>
  <p class="lede">In West Virginia, drivers under 18 get their license in three steps. Here is what the DMV says about each one.</p>

  <h2>Step 1: Instruction permit (age 15)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must be at least 15 and under 18.</li>
    <li>A parent with custody or a legal guardian must sign your application before you take the test.</li>
    <li>You take a knowledge test. The fee is $7.50 for each try.</li>
    <li>You may drive only between 5 a.m. and 10 p.m.</li>
    <li>You may have no more than two passengers who are not family, plus the supervising adult.</li>
    <li>No phone use or texting while driving. Police can stop you for it.</li>
    <li>The permit cannot be renewed. It ends on your 18th birthday, with a 30-day grace period.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Step 2: Intermediate license (age 16)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must be at least 16, have held your permit for 6 months, and have no tickets or other infractions in the 6 months before you apply.</li>
    <li>You need a form showing 50 hours of practice driving, with 10 of them at night. A parent or legal guardian signs it, or you can use a Driver Education Card.</li>
    <li>You take a road skills test. The fee is $7.50.</li>
    <li>You may drive alone between 5 a.m. and 10 p.m. From 10 p.m. to 5 a.m., a supervising adult must be with you, unless you are going to or from work, a school activity, a religious activity, or an emergency.</li>
    <li>For the first 6 months: no passengers under 20 who are not family. For the next 6 months: no more than one.</li>
    <li>No phone use or texting while driving.</li>
    <li>Two violations on this license mean you lose it until your 18th birthday.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Step 3: Full license (age 17)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must be at least 17 and have had your intermediate license for at least 1 year.</li>
    <li>You must have no infractions for 1 year. Headlamp and improper backing violations do not count.</li>
    <li>The fee is $5 for each year until your 21st birthday. The license runs out on your 21st birthday, with a 30-day grace period.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>The DMV page also links a free practice driving guide for parents and the free RoadReady app for logging hours. See the <a href={gdl}>DMV's graduated driver licensing page</a> for the full rules and the program flyer.</p>

  <h2>The DMV office in Morgantown</h2>
  {r('wv-dmv-morgantown-office') && <ResourceCard r={r('wv-dmv-morgantown-office')} />}

  <p>More for families: <a href={`${base}/family/`}>Family and life changes</a>.</p>

  <p class="meta">Rules from the <a href={gdl}>WV DMV graduated driver licensing page</a>, checked October 30, 2026. Rules and fees can change, so check the DMV page before you go. Something out of date? <a href={fixFormUrl({ page: Astro.url.pathname })}>Tell us</a>.</p>
</Base>
